<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>Long Bien by Motorbike: Motorbike Parking Guide in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Parking is the part of a Hanoi motorbike rental that guidebooks skip and riders do every single day, often several times a day. This page covers parking for riders based in Long Bien, the district on the east bank of the Red River where the rental from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu begins at 112 Nguyen Van Cu. Long Bien parks differently from the Old Quarter: it is a lived-in district with markets, schools and riverside roads rather than a wall-to-wall tourist zone, and that changes what a rider sees at the kerb. We describe the habits honestly, flag what varies street by street, and refuse to invent rules or guarantees no parking situation in Hanoi actually offers.</p>
<p>The plan is simple. We explain how parking works in Long Bien as a daily habit, where the practical anchors are, from the guesthouse or apartment you sleep in to the riverside pull-ups and market frontages, what the money and ticket customs look like, how overnight parking and longer stays change the question, what caution around locks and theft actually means, and which questions to ask at the counter before you ride off. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, and browse wider riding advice in the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>.</p>
